  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the statements separately.\n\n- Statement I is false. The graph of $y={h}^{′}(x)$ does not change sign around $x=-3$, therefore, there cannot be a relative extremum at this point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The slope of the tangent line to $y={h}^{′}(x)$ changes its sign somewhere near $x=1.$ Hence, the graph $y=h(x)$ has an inflection point inside $(0,2).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph of $y={h}^{′}(x)$ does not change sign around $x=2$, therefore, there cannot be a relative extremum at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
